{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CIB", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:400c10b861b90a4cc469cb1a9930a190e58902373ae67ae1f6ec3046e58b7ff3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe still have to develop the general machinery needed to say what\nit means for a morphism of algebraic stacks to have a given property\nat a point. For the moment the following lemma is sufficient.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e7a65e610c085079acafafef866cb96664964c8e09d14d57cddc40129b382874", "unit_id": "tag:0CIB:prose-0001"}
